{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "02C2", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\textit{Sets} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "TEXT_0001": "``big'' category"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{categories-remark-functors-sets-sets}\n", "suffix": "\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:895d17b74c9a401b0bcd0aaa3510f9b1222041f310979f86d90c15d5f82e2316", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:53d5f4f37dae1ba8f126b4a0fe3bdc45207ff28582c99d8c3c8977b64812f4be", "source_text": "This is one instance where the same thing does not hold if <MATH_0001> is a <TEXT_0001>. For example consider functors <MATH_0002>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:077f45cef101187b552174556513e37089cac087f05d6e4bf34b0c504dba5f99", "unit_id": "tag:02C2:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02C2", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:15294d70db53d08c95f055328b4323d11467ec27a4249a4d36fccaa0fa6ba706", "source_text": "As we have currently defined it such a functor is a class and not a set.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:63236717911a108fda0714902dec3a83b0165fd513eaed1142c60d0700b3aedf", "unit_id": "tag:02C2:p001"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02C2", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:15294d70db53d08c95f055328b4323d11467ec27a4249a4d36fccaa0fa6ba706", "source_text": "In other words, it is given by a formula in set theory (with some variables equal to specified sets)! It is not a good idea to try to consider all possible formulae of set theory as part of the definition of a mathematical object.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9eb5dd29901982f5ba4ab6bb49594f83cf7a2950a82059ca8e9affc6039a0d46", "unit_id": "tag:02C2:p002"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02C2", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{remark}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b2abdbe76f0db410dc827e846028d672900436ea305c9fc49249ba460ce8944d", "source_text": "The same problem presents itself when considering sheaves on the category of schemes for example. We will come back to this point later.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d16e56d37ec4f5ceb473fbfcb67a7e985035a4691800092c36e36ac162f33191", "unit_id": "tag:02C2:p003"}
